  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-01-05T14:39:15.669Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The avatar cloning feature is nice. But unfortunately, it has allowed unoptimized or malicious avatars to spread like a virus. There is seemingly no end to the amount of unoptimized stuff floating around in public now, completely unmoderated because they don't need a world to be spread.\n\nI propose a change to the cloning system: an avatar should only be cloneable if it's put in a world, and the world is approved for public at least once. When a world is marked for public and/or the optimization bot successfully checks it, a flag should be enabled on the avatar that allows other people to clone it.",
